al-semdial-2017/","tagSlugs":["/tags/natural-language-processing/","/tags/a-i/","/tags/deep-learning/"]},"frontmatter":{"title":"Review of SIGDial/SemDial 2017","tags":["Natural Language Processing","A.I.","Deep Learning"],"date":"2017-09-04T23:46:37.121"}}},{"node":{"fields":{"slug":"/posts/a-new-multiturn-dialogue-dataset/","tagSlugs":["/tags/natural-language-processing/","/tags/dataset/","/tags/dialogue/"]},"frontmatter":{"title":"A New Multi-Turn, Multi-Domain, Task-Oriented Dialogue Dataset","tags":["Natural Language Processing","Dataset","Dialogue"],"date":"2017-07-03T23:46:37.121"}}}]},"markdownRemark":{"id":"/Users/mihaileric/Documents/Projects/mihail911.github.io/src/pages/articles/2019-13-04---Support-Vector-Machines/index.md absPath of file >>> MarkdownRemark","html":"<figure>\n    \n  <a class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\" href=\"/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-2cb81.jpg\" style=\"display: block\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n  \n  <span class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\" style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n    <span class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\" style=\"padding-bottom: 51.29533678756477%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url(&apos;data:image/jpeg;base64,&apos;); background-size: cover; display: block;\">\n      <img class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\" alt=\"it&apos;s a support vector machine!\" title=\"\" src=\"/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-c6823.jpg\" srcset=\"/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-dad4f.jpg 240w,\n/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-1808a.jpg 480w,\n/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-c6823.jpg 960w,\n/static/svm_meme-5dd05bee673c663943d432afea4f5042-2cb81.jpg 1351w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\">\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    \n</figure>\n<p>In this post, we will explore a family of classification algorithms that has a very different theoretical\nmotivation from <a href=\"/posts/fundamentals-of-linear-regression\">ones</a> <a href=\"/posts/introduction-to-logistic-regression\">we’ve</a> <a href=\"/posts/not-so-naive-bayes\">seen</a> previously. We will be looking at <strong>support vector machines</strong>.</p>\n<p>Back in the early 2000s\nbefore deep learning surged to the forefront of AI, support vector machines were the cool kid on the block. Even today, support vector machines are still one of the best go-to algorithms\nfor a new classification task because of their powerful ability to represent very diverse types of statistical relationships in data as well as their ease of training.</p>\n<h2>Max-Margin Motivations</h2>\n<p>Let’s begin by motivating support vector machines. Recall our ridiculously overused classification problem: identifying whether a car is <strong>cheap</strong> or <strong>expensive</strong>, based on a set of features of that car.</p>\n<p>Imagine that we are plotting some of our data in 2-dimensional feature space. In other words, we are only\nextracting two features, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, from each car for building our model.  Furthermore, let’s label each point <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span> if it represents a car that is <strong>cheap</strong> and <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span> if it represents a car that is labelled <strong>expensive</strong>.</p>\n<p>We will try to\nlearn a linear model of our features, parameterized by the weights <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Our model will output <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span> if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_1\\cdot X_1 + W_2\\cdot X_2 &lt; 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> and <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span> if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_1\\cdot X_1 + W_2\\cdot X_2 &gt;= 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>This model will describe a linear separator of a collection of data. That linear separator of our data could look as follows:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-a3db2.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.5959595959596%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Linear separator of our data\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/linearSeparator1-af5113984a755c11f57170b4893cb5cc-a3db2.png 1584w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>Here the datapoints above the line are classified as <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span>, while those below are classified as <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span>. The important thing to see is that this is <em>only one</em> possible linear separator of the data.\nHowever, we could envision another separator that could separate the dataset into two colored halves just as well:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-064f7.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 58.875%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Alternative linear separator of our data\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/linearSeparator2-575ff7dd968141bd6ba5c89c6c49ca05-064f7.png 1600w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>In fact, there are an <em>infinite</em> number of possible separators that would split the data perfectly! How do we choose among them? </p>\n<p>Consider how we decided to label a datapoint as <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span> or <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span>. We computed <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_1\\cdot X_1 + W_2\\cdot X_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and said if it was negative, we labelled the point <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span>. Otherwise\nwe labelled it <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span>. Intuitively, it seems that if the quantity <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_1\\cdot X_1 + W_2\\cdot X_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.83333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.13889em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> for a given point is 15, we are more confident that it should\nbe <span style=\"color:red\">RED</span> than one for which the quantity is 1.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, the more negative the quantity is for a point the more confident we are that it should be <span style=\"color:blue\">BLUE</span>. In fact, we can use this value to\njudge our confidence for every single point!</p>\n<p>Geometrically, this confidence for a point’s label can be represented as the perpendicular distance from the point to the separator. Below we have designated the perpendicular distances\nto the separator for several sample points with the <span style=\"color:green\">GREEN</span> lines:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-2cca6.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.823677581863976%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Linear separator of our data with distances shown\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/linearSeparatorWithDistance-871279cdbd5513082473386d494de0fc-2cca6.png 1588w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>Now imagine if we took the minimum distance to the separator across all the points in the dataset. This minimum value is called the <strong>margin</strong>. Below we show the point that achieves the margin for the given separator:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-8d094.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.198998748435535%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Margin diagram\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/marginDiagram-8d629f6a92c562083e3f1631aa6cf9ce-8d094.png 1598w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>Optimal margins are at the core of support vector machine theory, and they inform how we will pick the “best” linear separator among the infinite choices. The way we will do this is by picking the linear separator that <strong>maximizes the margin</strong>.</p>\n<p>Put another way, each separator defines a certain margin (i.e. an associated minimum perpendicular distance\nto the separator). Then, among the infinite possible separators, we will pick the separator that maximizes the margin.</p>\n<p>Make sure you really understand that last statement!\nSupport vector machines are often called <strong>max-margin classifiers</strong> for that exact reason. Given an optimal margin linear separator, the points with the smallest margins that are closest to the linear separator are called the <strong>support vectors</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Training the SVM</h2>\n<p>So, how do we train a support vector machine? The full mathematical details to describe the cost function we want to optimize are a bit beyond the scope of this post, but we will\ngive a brief description of the training cost function.</p>\n<p>Given a collection of datapoints <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[(X_1, Y_1), (X_2, Y_2), ... , (X_n, Y_n)]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.75em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.22222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.22222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.151392em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.151392em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.22222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span> (where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.68333em;vertical-align:0em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span></span></span></span> are the input features\nand <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.68333em;vertical-align:0em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span></span></span></span> are the correct output labels) and a vector of weights <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.68333em;vertical-align:0em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span></span></span></span> for our input features, finding the optimal margin classifier amounts to solving</p>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>min</mtext><mi>W</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\textrm{min}_W \\frac{1}{2} ||W||^2 </annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.32144em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:2.00744em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\">min</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.32833099999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.32144em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.15em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"stretchy\" style=\"height:0.2em;\"><svg width='400em' height='0.2em' viewBox='0 0 400000 200' preserveAspectRatio='xMinYMin slice'><path d='M0 80H400000 v40H0z M0 80H400000 v40H0z'/></svg></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641079999999999em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mtext>such that </mtext><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\textrm{such that } Y_i(W^TX_i) \\geq 1 \\textrm{ for all } i = 1, ..., n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8913309999999999em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:1.1413309999999999em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\">such that </span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.22222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913309999999999em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\"> for all </span></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">i</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">n</span></span></span></span></span>\n<p>This cost function is basically a fancy way of saying that we want maximize the margin, while ensuring the margin of each datapoint is greater than or equal to 1.</p>\n<p>It turns out finding the optimum for this cost function is a convex optimization problem, which means there exist standard algorithms for solving the problem. This is good news\nfor us because it means optimally training a support vector machine is a tractable problem!</p>\n<p>As a point of comparison, there exist some problems for\nwhich we cannot find the optimal value in a computationally reasonable time. It may even take exponential time to find the optimum!</p>\n<h2>The Kernel Trick</h2>\n<p>Thus far we have motivated support vector machines by only focusing on linear separators of data.\nIt turns out that support vector machines can actually learn nonlinear separators, which is why they are such a powerful model class!</p>\n<p>To motivate this idea,\nimagine that we have an input point with three features <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X = (X_1, X_2, X_3)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.75em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. We can transform the 3-dimensional vector <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.68333em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.68333em;vertical-align:0em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span></span></span></span> into a higher-dimensional\nvector by applying a transformation function as follows: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T(X) = (X_1, X_2, X_3, X_1\\cdot X_1, X_2\\cdot X_2, X_3\\cdot X_3)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.75em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">T</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.30110799999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>Our transformation function did two things:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>it created a 6-dimensional vector from a 3-dimensional one </li>\n<li>it added nonlinear interactions in our features by having certain new features be the squares of the original features.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Transforming features into a higher-dimensional space has some perks, namely that some data which is not linearly separable in a certain-dimensional space could become\nlinearly separable when we project it into the higher-dimensional space.</p>\n<p>As a motivating example, consider the following data which is not linearly separable in 2-d space:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-db234.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.64912280701754%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Kernel trick not separable diagram\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/kernelTrickNotSeparableDiagram-5e4b923f8edecc6c4c626ecc5824b763-db234.png 1596w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>which becomes separable in 3-dimensional space through an appropriate feature transformation:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-e795c.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 60.97922848664689%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Kernel trick separable diagram\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/kernelTrickSeparableDiagram-a269b8bb071acaf2052ade148b81ff3b-e795c.png 1348w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>Such input feature transformations are particularly useful in support vector machines. It turns out that support vector machines formalize the notion of these feature transformation function through something called a <strong>kernel</strong>.</p>\n<p>Without getting too much into the mathematical details, a kernel allows a support vector machine to learn using these transformed features in higher-dimensional space in a much more computationally efficient way. This is called the <strong>kernel trick</strong>.</p>\n<p>Examples of kernels that are frequently used when learning a support vector machine\nmodel include the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polynomial_kernel\">polynomial kernel</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radial_basis_function_kernel\">radial basis function kernel</a>.</p>\n<p>A really crazy mathematical property of the radial\nbasis function is that it can be interpreted as a mapping for an infinite-dimensional feature space! And yet we can still use it to do effective learning\nin our models. That’s insane</p>\n<h2>Slacking Off</h2>\n<p>Thus far, we have assumed that the data we are working with is always linearly separable. And if it wasn’t to begin with, we assumed we could project it into a higher-dimensional feature space where it would be linearly separable and the kernel trick would do all the heavy lifting.</p>\n<p>However, our data may not always be linearly separable. We may find ourselves in a situation as follows where it is impossible to linearly separate the data:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-6b4e7.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.2964824120603%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Not linearly separable data diagram\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/nonlinearlySeparableDiagram-31ba4f0cdba4b759b6020ec590c95884-6b4e7.png 1592w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>Moreover, recall that our original support vector machine cost function enforced the constraint that every point needs to have a margin greater than or equal to 1.</p>\n<p>But perhaps this condition is too strict for all cases. For example, enforcing this condition for all points may make our model very susceptible to outliers as follows:</p>\n<p>\n  <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-a3db2.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n  \n  <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n    style=\"position: relative; display: block; ; max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\"\n  >\n    <span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n      style=\"padding-bottom: 59.5959595959596%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n    >\n      <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; margin: 0; vertical-align: middle; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; box-shadow: inset 0px 0px 0px 400px white;\"\n        alt=\"Support vector machine outlier diagram\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-3d61e.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-d182c.png 240w,\n/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-5220f.png 480w,\n/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-3d61e.png 960w,\n/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-6fd10.png 1440w,\n/static/svmOutlierDiagram-dbef9a2e874968a10f9a8c1b82338375-a3db2.png 1584w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n      />\n    </span>\n  </span>\n  \n  </a>\n    </p>\n<p>To combat this problem, we can introduce what are called <strong>slack penalties</strong> into our support vector machine objective that allow certain points to have margins potentially smaller than 1. With these penalties, our new cost looks as follows:</p>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>min</mtext><mi>W</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>⋅</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\textrm{min}_W \\frac{1}{2} ||W||^2  + K \\cdot \\sum_i s_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.32144em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:2.599109em;vertical-align:-1.277669em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\">min</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.32833099999999993em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.32144em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.15em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"stretchy\" style=\"height:0.2em;\"><svg width='400em' height='0.2em' viewBox='0 0 400000 200' preserveAspectRatio='xMinYMin slice'><path d='M0 80H400000 v40H0z M0 80H400000 v40H0z'/></svg></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641079999999999em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07153em;\">K</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0500050000000003em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.872331em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.050005em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.277669em;\"></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><mtext>such that </mtext><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\textrm{such that } Y_i(W^TX_i) \\geq 1-s_i \\textrm{ for all } i = 1, ..., n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8913309999999999em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:1.1413309999999999em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\">such that </span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.22222em;\">Y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.22222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">W</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8913309999999999em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">T</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\" style=\"margin-right:0.07847em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:-0.07847em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222222222222222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\"> for all </span></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">i</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">n</span></span></span></span></span>\n<span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_i \\geq 0 \\textrm{ for all } i = 1, ..., m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.69444em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.8888799999999999em;vertical-align:-0.19444em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord textrm\"> for all </span></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">i</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.2777777777777778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"margin-right:0.16666666666666666em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathit\">m</span></span></span></span></span>\n<p>Here the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.43056em;\"></span><span class=\"strut bottom\" style=\"height:0.58056em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathit\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.31166399999999994em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.5500000000000003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathit mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are our slack variables. Notice that we have changed the expression we are trying to minimize. The value <strong>K</strong> is\nwhat is called a <em>hyperparameter</em>.</p>\n<p>In a nutshell, this means we can adjust <strong>K</strong> to determine how much we want our model to focus on minimizing the new term in our cost function or the old term.\nThis is our first example of a very important concept in machine learning called <strong>regularization</strong>.</p>\n<p>We will discuss regularization in a lot more detail in the next section. For now, just understand that this new addition makes the support vector machine\nmore robust to nonlinearly-separable data.</p>\n<h2>Final Thoughts</h2>\n<p>Support vector machines are very powerful model. They are great for handling linearly separable data and with their various extensions\ncan adequately handle nonlinearly separable data scenarios</p>\n<p>As part of the machine learning toolkit, it is a great go-to model to try when\nstarting on a new problem. However, one of its downsides is that using certain kernels, such as the radial basis function kernel, can sometimes make the model\ntraining slower, so be wary of that.</p>","fields":{"tagSlugs":["/tags/machine-learning/","/tags/a-i/","/tags/data-science/"]},"frontmatter":{"title":"Basics of Support Vector Machines","tags":["Machine Learning","A.I.","Data Science"],"date":"2019-04-20T23:46:37.121","description":"We discuss support vector machines, a very powerful and versatile machine learning model."}}},"pathContext":{"slug":"/posts/support-vector-machines/"}}


